# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HARD RULE: no WRDS-derived content in git, ever. No data files, no forecast
# parquets. Only code, configs, the small checkpoint-coupled id maps, and the
# Forma checkpoints live in the repo.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Anchored to the repo root ON PURPOSE. An unanchored `data/` also matches the
# package's own `src/forma/data/` subpackage, which silently kept the tuple
# dataset, transforms and config helpers out of the repo -- a clone could not
# even import the model. The extension globs below are the real guard against
# WRDS-derived content: they apply at any depth regardless of directory name.
/data/
/results/
/forecasts/
*.parquet
*.csv

# ...except the two SMALL checkpoint-coupled categorical id maps (schema/metadata,
# NOT firm-level data): the account and industry name->embedding-index tables the
# shipped Forma checkpoints were trained under. Deriving these from data ordering
# at inference time silently permutes the embeddings, so they MUST ship.
!src/forma/metadata/account_id_map.csv
!src/forma/metadata/industry_id_map.csv

# ...and any aggregate-level (by-horizon / by-quarter) CSVs committed to render
# the F1/F2 figures. Firm-level CSVs stay ignored by the rule above.
!results_panels/**/*.csv

# WRDS credentials must never be committed.
.pgpass
*.pgpass
*.env

# LLM benchmark: never commit responses, API keys, or forecast outputs.
scripts/llm/responses/
*.responses.jsonl

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Editors / OS
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
